Z||000000||varnster||11-06-2001||09:02 PM||||How do you get the trim lose, I think it just has those plastic push fastners but not<BR>sure, I dont want to brake it.Any tips?||||reg||9
Z||000001||California Kid||11-06-2001||11:19 PM||||Just pull it off, clips might break, but you can still get them from dealer.||||reg||1
Z||000002||btoth||11-06-2001||11:21 PM||||What are you trying to remove it to do?  I think to completely remove it, you have to loosen the B-pillar trim as well.  When I replaced those little clips with new ones, I just pulled it down far enough to reach my hand in there to get the old ones out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-07-2001||01:54 AM||||At the top (above the door), there are two pressed in tabs.  The metal part that the plastic on the A pillar trim is pushed into is screwed on to the frame.  It seems to be easiest if you just unscrew the metal part.||||reg||1
